# Barangay Portal — Project Rules

## Project overview
A static, dependency-free frontend prototype of a Philippine barangay resident portal.
Residents sign in, request certificates (barangay clearance, residency, indigency),
track request status, and view how the barangay budget is spent.

## Tech stack
- Vanilla HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript (ES5-compatible style, no framework)
- No build step, no bundler, no package manager
- Fonts loaded from Google Fonts: `Bricolage Grotesque`, `Source Sans 3`
- Files: `index.html`, `styles.css`, `app.js` (flat, at repo root)

## Running
Open `index.html` directly in a browser, or serve the folder statically:
`python -m http.server 8000`

## Architecture
- Single page with two views: `#login` and `#app`, toggled via the `hidden` attribute.
- `#app` has four tab sections (`home`, `cert`, `budget`, `arch`); the `tab(t)` function
  is the single router — it sets `aria-selected` on tab buttons and toggles section visibility.
- `app.js` uses a `$` helper (`document.getElementById`) instead of `querySelector`.
- All mock data lives in module-scope arrays at the top of `app.js`: `types`, `reqs`,
  `budget`, `projs`. Derive totals from these arrays, never hardcode sums.
- Rendering is plain template literals assigned to `innerHTML`, with a re-render
  function per view (`renderReqs()`, `preview()`, etc.).
- Navigation between tabs is triggered by `data-go="<tab>"` attributes, delegated in JS.

## Code style (follow existing conventions)
- Compact, dense formatting: no spaces around operators or inside braces,
  multiple declarations per line, CSS rules packed onto one line.
- Prefer `var`/`function()` over `let`/`const`/`arrow` in `app.js` to match the file.
- CSS: one rule per line, custom properties from `:root` for all colors — never hardcode
  hex values outside `:root` unless it is a deliberate non-token shade (e.g. `.paper`).
- Prefer terse class names already in use (`.btn`, `.card`, `.mute`, `.pill`, `.bar`, `.row`).
- Keep the semantic color palette (`--pri`, `--red`, `--sun`, `--c1`..`--c5`) intact.

## Frontend guidelines
- Mobile-first, works from ~320px up; `max-width:960px` centered containers.
- Respect safe-area insets (`env(safe-area-inset-top/-bottom)`) on the header, nav, and html.
- Accessible by default: keep `aria-selected`, `role`, `label`/`for` pairs,
  `alt`-equivalent text, and the visible `:focus-visible` outline intact.
- Placeholders like `[Pangalan]`, `[City / Municipality]`, `[Punong Barangay Name]`
  are intentional placeholders for the real barangay — do not "fix" them unless asked.
- No `alert()`/`confirm()` for user feedback; use the in-page `.mute` / status message elements.

## Constraints
- Do not add dependencies, frameworks, or a build system unless explicitly requested.
- Escape or use `textContent` for any value that comes from user input before
  inserting it into HTML (`app.js` already does this for the certificate preview).
- Never commit secrets, API keys, or real resident PII. Everything here is mock data.
- Keep changes to existing files minimal and consistent; avoid unrelated refactors.

## Workflow
- Branch off `main` for features, commit with short imperative messages
  (e.g. `Add certificate request filters`).
- Before pushing, verify the page still works in the browser and that no console errors appear.